## Types

The back-index is one remote timer `Trigger` per bot in a space, whose input names everything a run needs.

```mdl
type BackIndexInput
  desc: The trigger's input; ConfigureBackIndex writes it and CrawlDiscordChannels reads it.
  fields:
    applicationId: string             # the Discord app (bot) installed in the server
    accessToken?: Ref<AccessToken>    # the bot's token; absent for Kai, whose token EDGE holds
    channels: string[]                # top-level Discord channel ids to crawl
    descendThreads?: boolean          # default true
    maxDays?: number                  # lookback for a channel crawled for the first time
    maxDepth?: number
    maxSteps?: number                 # pages one run reads; default 2
    state: Ref<CrawlState>
    facts: Ref<Feed>
```

The bot host answers messages in Discord's own field names, trimmed to what the crawl maps; nothing else of the API
response crosses.

```mdl
type DiscordMessage
  fields:
    id: string
    type: number
    content: string
    timestamp: string
    author: { id: string, username: string, global_name?: string }
    mentions: { id: string, username: string, global_name?: string }[]
    referencedMessageId?: string
    thread?: { id: string, name: string }
```

```mdl
type DiscordSourceChannel
  fields:
    id: string
    name: string
    guildId: string
    guildName: string
```

## Services

```mdl
service DiscordBotService
  desc: |
    plugin-discord's bot service, gaining the two source calls a crawl reads through. The app reaches it over EDGE's
    `/discord/bots/:applicationId` routes, signed with the user's identity; a plugin bundle on EDGE reaches it over
    compute-service's `DISCORD_BOT` service. Both end at the bot host, which signs the Discord call with the bot's
    token.
  ops:
    listChannels(bot: { applicationId: string, spaceId: string }) → DiscordSourceChannel[]
    fetchMessages(bot: { applicationId: string, spaceId: string }, channelId: string, after: string, limit: number) → DiscordMessage[]
  errors:
    DiscordBotError: the bot does not serve the space, is not running, or the channel is outside the servers the space connected
```

## Operations

```mdl
op ConfigureBackIndex
  key: org.dxos.operation.discord.configureBackIndex
  desc: Creates or updates the space's back-index for a bot: its CrawlState, its fact feed and the remote timer trigger.
  input:
    applicationId: string
    accessToken?: Ref<AccessToken>
    channels: string[]
    trigger?: Ref<Trigger>        # the back-index to reconfigure; a new one when absent
    name?: string
    cron?: string                 # default every two minutes
    enabled?: boolean
  output: { trigger: Ref<Trigger>, state: Ref<CrawlState>, facts: Ref<Feed> }
  effects: [echo:read, echo:write]
```

```mdl
op CrawlDiscordChannels
  key: org.dxos.operation.discord.crawlChannels
  desc: One bounded run of the back-index, as the trigger invokes it.
  input: BackIndexInput
  output: { done: boolean, errored: number, steps: number, messages: number, error?: string }
  effects: [echo:read, echo:write, ai]
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Setup from the Discord companion

  req F-1.1: The agent's Discord companion shows, on every channel of a server the bot is in, whether the channel is indexed and a toggle that adds it to or removes it from the space's back-index for that bot.

  req F-1.2: The first toggle creates the back-index with ConfigureBackIndex; later toggles update its channels in place, so a space has one back-index per bot.

  req F-1.3: Removing the last channel disables the trigger and keeps its CrawlState and fact feed.

  req F-1.4: Setup asks for no token when the bot is Kai.
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Pipeline

  req F-2.1: A run is DiscordPipeline's assembly, with the same stages as the Discord facts CLI: persist message, agent profile, extract questions, extract facts, topics, answer questions.

  req F-2.2: Only the stores differ from the CLI: the frontier and cursors live in the CrawlState ECHO object, facts go to the fact feed, and Topics and Persons are written to the space.

  req F-2.3: Facts move from the fact feed to the space's memory service once it exists, with no change to the stages.

  req F-2.4: A run reads at most maxSteps pages and resumes from the CrawlState on the next trigger, so a message read again unchanged costs no model call.
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Reading as the bot
  uses: [DiscordBotService, DiscordMessage, DiscordSourceChannel]

  req F-3.1: The crawl's Discord source is built only on DiscordBotService.listChannels and fetchMessages; no Discord API request, path or header crosses from a plugin to the bot host.

  req F-3.2: The bot host answers listChannels with the text and announcement channels of the servers in which the space has connected a channel, and nothing for any other server the bot is in.

  req F-3.3: The bot host answers fetchMessages only for a channel or thread in one of those servers, with at most `limit` messages after `after`, oldest first.

  req F-3.4: The bot host refuses both calls for a space that does not own the bot.

  req F-3.5: compute-service refuses a call whose bot names a space other than the invocation's own.
```

```mdl
feat F-4: Token custody

  req F-4.1: Kai's token never leaves the bot host: not to compute-service, not to a plugin bundle, not to the app, and not into the space.

  req F-4.2: For a bot that is not Kai, the space holds its AccessToken and the trigger names it by reference; the bot host reads the token from the space by id.

  req F-4.3: No answer of the bot host carries a token, an authorization header or a raw Discord API response.
```

```mdl
feat F-5: Failures

  req F-5.1: A run never fails its invocation: its error and outcome are written to the CrawlState, so they outlive the run.

  req F-5.2: A source call the bot host refuses marks the channel as errored in the CrawlState with the host's reason, and the run carries on with the other channels.
```

```mdl
feat F-6: Pipeline panel

  req F-6.1: Brain's Pipeline panel reads the back-index's state from its ECHO objects (the CrawlState, the trigger and the fact feed), not from a file the CLI wrote.
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
scenario T-1: Index a channel with Kai
  given: a space whose agent has a channel of the DXOS server connected through Kai; no back-index
  when: the person toggles Index on #general in the Discord companion
  then:
    - one Trigger, CrawlState and fact feed exist, the trigger's input naming Kai's application id and #general, and no AccessToken
    - the next run appends facts to the feed and writes Topics to the space
```

```mdl
scenario T-2: A server the space did not connect
  given: Kai is in the DXOS server and another server; the space connected a channel of the DXOS server only
  when: a crawl asks fetchMessages for a channel of the other server
  then:
    - the bot host refuses it and Discord is not called
    - the channel is marked errored in the CrawlState with the host's reason
```

```mdl
scenario T-3: Another space names the bot
  given: Kai's bot host owned by space A
  when: a crawl in space B calls fetchMessages naming space A
  then:
    - compute-service refuses the call before it reaches the bot host
```

```mdl
scenario T-4: Stop indexing
  given: a back-index with one channel
  when: the person toggles Index off on that channel
  then:
    - the trigger is disabled, with no channels
    - the CrawlState and fact feed are kept
```

## Changelog

```mdl
decision D-1: The plugin's back-index runs pipeline-discord's DiscordPipeline with the same stages as the CLI, with different dependencies injected. Its crawl state is an ECHO object, and it will eventually write into the space's memory service.
  date: 2026-11-18
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2]
```

```mdl
decision D-2: The Pipeline panel takes the back-index's state from its ECHO objects.
  date: 2026-11-18
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-6]
```

```mdl
decision D-3: Extraction is set up the way agents are: install Composer's Discord bot (Kai) in the server from the Discord companion. The crawl and ConfigureBackIndex take the bot's application id and, for a bot that is not Kai, its access token, as BindChannel does, in place of a Connection. The crawl reads Discord through discord-service, which adds Kai's token. The companion gets a per-channel choice to index that calls ConfigureBackIndex.
  date: 2026-11-18
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1, F-3, F-4, BackIndexInput, ConfigureBackIndex, CrawlDiscordChannels]
  why: A space then holds no token for Kai, and indexing is one more choice next to connecting a channel to the agent.
  rejected: A bot token pasted into a Connection, which puts a bot token in every space that indexes.
```

```mdl
decision D-4: Approve [D-3].
  date: 2026-11-18
  by: user:dmaretskyi
```

```mdl
decision D-5: Kai's token is not exposed to operations; discord-service exposes a semantic source for the pipeline rather than a passthrough of Discord API requests.
  date: 2026-11-18
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-3, F-4, DiscordBotService]
```

```mdl
decision D-6: The source is two calls, listChannels and fetchMessages, answering Discord's message fields trimmed to what the crawl maps, and scoped to the servers in which the space has connected a channel. Fills in [D-5].
  date: 2026-11-18
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-3.1, F-3.2, F-3.3, F-4.3, DiscordMessage, DiscordSourceChannel]
  why: These are the only two Discord reads the crawler's Source makes. Scoping by connected servers stops an owning space from reading every server the shared Kai app is in.
  rejected: A GET-only passthrough checked against the space, which lets the owning space read any guild, member list or user Kai can see.
```

```mdl
decision D-7: compute-service refuses a source call whose bot names a space other than the invocation's. Fills in [D-5].
  date: 2026-11-18
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-3.5]
  why: The space in the call is the caller's to write; without the check a bundle in one space reads as another space's bot.
```

```mdl
decision D-8: A refused source call marks the channel as errored with the host's reason, and removing the last indexed channel disables the trigger rather than deleting the back-index. Fills in [D-3].
  date: 2026-11-18
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1.3, F-5.2]
  why: The crawler isolates a failed target so the others continue; keeping the CrawlState lets re-indexing resume from its cursors.
```

```mdl
question Q-1: Kai's bot host serves one owner space per EDGE environment. How do other spaces index through Kai?
  date: 2026-11-18
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-3.4, F-1.4]
  options:
    - Owner only: one space per environment indexes through Kai; others bring their own bot and token.
    - Per-guild owners: the bot host keys ownership by server, so each server belongs to the space that connected it.
```
